# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles must keep LF line endings. A Windows checkout with autocrlf rewrites them to CRLF, and a
# container entrypoint with a CRLF shebang fails with "no such file or directory" (the carriage return becomes part of
# the interpreter name).
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.mp4 binary
*.png binary
# Line endings and binaries, enforced on every machine (autocrlf corrupted PDFs and left shell scripts and Dockerfiles CRLF, 2026-10-13).
*.bash text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.gif binary
/edge/Dockerfile text eol=lf
/hub/Dockerfile text eol=lf
